---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Definition Lists">
  <div class="test-container" style="padding: 2rem;">
    <h1 class="text-chapter" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">Definition Lists</h1>

    <p style="max-width: 60ch;">
      Element styles for <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;dt&gt;</code>, and
      <code>&lt;dd&gt;</code>, scoped under <code>main</code>. Terms render as
      mono uppercase captions; definitions as body text. Layout (stacked vs.
      inline strip) is owned by the consuming page — the design system styles
      only the elements.
    </p>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 class="text-section" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Stacked (default flow)
      </h2>
      <div
        style="padding: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--freefall-border-subtle); border-radius: 4px;"
      >
        <dl>
          <dt>System</dt>
          <dd>FREE//FALL 0.7.x</dd>
          <dt>Length</dt>
          <dd>One-shot, 3–5 hours</dd>
          <dt>Players</dt>
          <dd>3–5</dd>
          <dt>Content warnings</dt>
          <dd>Violence, body horror, isolation &amp; confinement</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div
        style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--freefall-text-muted); font-family: var(--freefall-font-mono); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0.5rem;"
      >
        dt: var(--freefall-font-mono) 0.75rem uppercase
        var(--freefall-text-muted)<br />
        dd: var(--freefall-text-body), margin-bottom 2 *
        var(--freefall-space-1)
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 class="text-section" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Inline strip (page-level flex layout)
      </h2>
      <div
        style="padding: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--freefall-border-subtle); border-radius: 4px;"
      >
        <dl style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin: 0;">
          <div>
            <dt>System</dt>
            <dd>FREE//FALL 0.7.x</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Length</dt>
            <dd>One-shot, 3–5 hours</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Players</dt>
            <dd>3–5</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div
        style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--freefall-text-muted); font-family: var(--freefall-font-mono); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0.5rem;"
      >
        Wrapper divs group each pair; the flex layout is inline page style,
        not a design-system rule.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 class="text-section" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Stat aside (scenario metadata)
      </h2>
      <p style="max-width: 60ch;">
        A stat table never sits on top of the page heading — it rides the
        content grid's <code>content-side</code> column as an
        <code>&lt;aside&gt;</code>, beside the prose. On layouts too narrow
        for the side column it falls back to the inline strip above the
        content (the grid places <code>.content-side</code> back in the main
        column). Used by the scenario overview in apps/free-fall.
      </p>
      <div
        style="padding: 2rem; border: 1px solid var(--freefall-border-subtle); border-radius: 4px; max-width: 28ch;"
      >
        <dl
          style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--freefall-border-subtle); padding-left: 1rem;"
        >
          <div>
            <dt>Type</dt>
            <dd style="margin: 0;">Demo (one-shot)</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>System</dt>
            <dd style="margin: 0;">FREE//FALL 0.7.x</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Length</dt>
            <dd style="margin: 0;">3–5 hours</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Players</dt>
            <dd style="margin: 0;">3–5</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div
        style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--freefall-text-muted); font-family: var(--freefall-font-mono); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0.5rem;"
      >
        &lt;aside class="content-side"&gt; direct child of .content-grid ·
        side tier: stacked pairs, border-left var(--freefall-border-subtle)
        · base tier fallback: the inline strip above, border-bottom instead.
        Tier thresholds come from content-grid.css, not this component.
        <br /><br />
        Foot-gun: an aside placed BEFORE the content it flanks must pin
        itself with grid-row: 1 in the side tier — an auto-placed first
        child claims row 1 and the auto-flow cursor never backtracks, so
        everything after it starts on row 2, below the aside instead of
        beside it.
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
